WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.234
-I'm a big fan of your work

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.968
and I'm so happy to meet you.
-Well, likewise.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.801
-You're a stud.
Everyone loves ya. Yeah.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:07.834
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.300
-Flattery will get you
everywhere.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.033
-Yeah. I want to talk
about "House of the Dragon,"

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:15.033
but I also want to talk
about, on "The Crown,"

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.234
-Whoo!
-you played Prince -- Yeah.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.868
I mean, oh, my God.
Prince Philip.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:20.100
[ Cheering and applause ]
You did such a great job

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.467
as Prince Philip.
-Thank you.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.400
Nominated for awards
and all this stuff.
-Yeah.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.968
Always the bridesmaid.
I never win.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.434
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:28.667
It's cooler
to just be nominated.
-Is it?

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.234
-Yeah.
-You've won loads,
though, ain't ya?

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.834
-No, I've never been nominated.
-What?!

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:32.767
[ Laughter ]
-But I'm just saying.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.267
But it sounds cool.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:36.534
Did you ever meet any
of the royals

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:37.601
-[ Inhales sharply ]
-or did you meet the queen?

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.901
-I met Harry.
No, I mean not the queen.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:43.400
I met Harry. I met William.
I met now-King Charles.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.501
-Wow!
-Yeah, he came to "Doctor Who."

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:47.734
He was impeccably dressed.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:49.033
And I went,
"You're very well-dressed,"

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.767
and he went, "No, no,
you're very well-dressed."

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.033
And I went,
"You've got marvelous shoes."

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.501
He went, "Actually, you've got
marvelous shoes."

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.267
And I went, "They're red,"
and he went,

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.267
"But yours are red."

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.267
-Wow!
-And I went,

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.100
"How long have you had yours?"

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.667
And he said, "35 years."

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:00.434
[ Laughter ]
-No!

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.534
Thirty-five years.

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.200
-He had his shoes for 35 years?
-Yeah.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.100
You'd think, as a king,
he'd be able to, you know...

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.701
-Yeah, exactly.
-...afford a new pair of boots,

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.367
you know what I mean?
-Get a new pair of shoes.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.667
Uh --
-Oh, yes!

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.801
-Lookit, this is a photo
of you guys in front of the --

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.868
-No, I look like
I've won a prize.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:16.467
Do you know what I mean?

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.534
